       --bb _n_a_m_e, ----bbaassiiss--nnaammee==_n_a_m_e
              Preload compression basis _n_a_m_e into FIASCO.  The basis _n_a_m_e pro‐
              vides the initial compression dictionary.  Either use one of the
              files "small.fco", "medium.fco", or "large.fco" that  come  with
              ppnnmmttooffiiaassccoo  or create a new ASCII basis file.


       --zz _N, ----ooppttiimmiizzee==_N
              Set  optimization  level to _N.  Level is 0 (fastest) to 3 (slow‐
              est); default is 1.  Be warned, the encoding  time  dramatically
              increased when _N=22 or _N=33 while the compression performance only
              slightly improves.


       --PP, ----pprreeddiiccttiioonn
              Use additional predictive coding.  If this optimization  is  en‐
              abled  then  the image is compressed in two steps.  In the first
              step, a coarse approximation of  the  image  is  computed  using
              large  unichrome  blocks.   Finally, the delta image is computed
              and the prediction error is approximated using the standard  FI‐
              ASCO algorithm.


       --DD _N, ----ddiiccttiioonnaarryy--ssiizzee==_N
              Set  size  of  dictionary that is used when coding the luminance
              band to _N; default is 10000, i.e., the  dictionary  is  not  re‐
              stricted.


       --CC _N, ----cchhrroommaa--ddiiccttiioonnaarryy==_N
              Set  size of dictionary that is used when coding chroma bands to
              _N; default is 40.


       --QQ _N, ----cchhrroommaa--qqffaaccttoorr==_N
              Reduce the quality of chroma band compression _N-times  with  re‐
              spect  to  the user defined quality _q of the luminance band com‐
              pression (----qquuaalliittyy=_q); default is 2.


       --tt _N, ----ttiilliinngg--eexxppoonneenntt==_N
              Subdivide the image into 2^_N tiles prior coding; default  is  4,
              i.e. the image is subdivided into 16 tiles. The processing order
              of the individual tiles  is  defined  by  the  option  ----ttiilliinngg--
              mmeetthhoodd==_n_a_m_e.


       --TT _n_a_m_e, ----ttiilliinngg--mmeetthhoodd==_n_a_m_e
              Order  the individual image tiles (the image is subdivided into;
              see option ----ttiilliinngg--eexxppoonneenntt==_N) by method _n_a_m_e; default is ddeesscc--
              vvaarriiaannccee.



